<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zimbabwe African People's Union</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as ZAPU</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a> African People's Union (ZAPU) was a nationalist movement founded in 1961 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joshua-nkomo">Joshua Nkomo</a> to oppose white minority rule in Southern Rhodesia. Its armed wing, ZIPRA, fought the Rhodesian government from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a>. After independence it was persecuted during the Gukurahundi massacres in Matabeleland and merged with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe-african-national-union">ZANU</a> in 1987.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zimbabwe-african-peoples-union.jpg" alt="Zimbabwe African People's Union" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Xophe84 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zimbabwe_African_People%27s_Union_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
